h('3 Methodology',1)
h('3.1 Research Design and Method Applied',2)
para('The proposal specifies a quantitative experimental study. The empirical design is a controlled, repeated-run comparison in an isolated simulation or authorised cyber-physical testbed. Every detector is evaluated against the same labelled scenario matrix and data collection procedure. The present research work applies that methodology in two completed stages: documentary analysis of the proposal, baseline paper, and relevant Nigerian and technical sources; and a design-stage operationalisation of the variables, framework, scenarios, metrics, and analysis plan. No experiment was executed for this report because the supplied material did not include testbed access, experimental logs, or a labelled dataset. Consequently, the research method is specified and applied to the evidence synthesis, while primary hypotheses await testbed validation.')
para('The documentary analysis was directed by the proposal’s alignment requirements. The baseline was examined for its attack classes, protocol, architecture, signals, stated challenges, and evaluation logic. Nigerian context sources were included where they establish sector control-system integration, power-system operating characteristics, national cybersecurity priorities, or sector-specific cybersecurity analysis. Technical standards were used to constrain safety claims. The output is a testable protocol rather than a simulated result set.')

h('3.2 Test Environment and System Boundary',2)
para('The future experiment should use either an emulation-based cyber-physical testbed or a simulator that synchronises a power-flow or dynamic grid model with a communication and control stack. A suitable architecture includes a control-centre master, field/outstation endpoints, a protocol communication network, a grid simulator, monitoring sensors, time synchronisation, and an isolated attack injector. DNP3 is the first protocol target to preserve direct comparability with Wlazlo et al. (2021). Nigerian research partners may select another locally available protocol in a separate protocol-specific phase. The exact simulator, topology, protocol implementation, host specifications, and sampling interval must be recorded before data generation.')
para('The test environment must be isolated from utility and public networks, use synthetic or explicitly authorised data, and prevent any control packet from reaching live infrastructure. It should have immutable experiment logs, a documented clock source, repeatable random seeds, and a safe reset procedure. The operating envelope and permitted mitigation actions must be approved by the testbed owner before any attack scenario is executed.')

h('3.3 Variables and Operational Measures',2)
